CAT = "s24Discipline"; SEG = "DIS"
Q = [
("A firm's own review concludes that a representative's misconduct violated securities rules and had widespread effect. Under Rule 4530(b) the firm must:",
 'Report it to FINRA within 30 calendar days', ['Report it only if a customer complains', 'Wait for FINRA to discover it on exam', 'Report it with the year-end audit'],
 'Rule 4530(b) requires a member to report, within 30 calendar days after it concludes or reasonably should have concluded, that it or an associated person violated securities laws or rules; Supplementary Material .01 limits this to conduct with widespread or potential widespread impact or other significant conduct.'),
('A customer sends a written complaint alleging that her representative forged her signature on a withdrawal form for $900. The firm must:',
 'Report it under Rule 4530 regardless of the amount', ['Report it only if the loss is over $5,000', 'Resolve it before deciding whether to report', 'Report it only if the customer files for arbitration'],
 'Rule 4530(a)(1)(B) requires reporting any written customer complaint alleging theft, misappropriation or forgery. No dollar threshold applies to that trigger.'),
('Rule 4530(d) statistical data on customer complaints received in a calendar quarter is due by:',
 'The 15th day of the month after the quarter', ['The last business day of the same calendar quarter', '30 days after each complaint arrives', "The firm's annual audit date"],
 'Rule 4530(d) requires members to report statistical and summary information on written customer complaints quarterly, by the 15th day of the month following the calendar quarter in which they were received.'),
("A member firm settles a customer's damages claim against the firm itself. Under Rule 4530(a)(1)(G) it must report the settlement if it exceeds:",
 '$25,000', ['$5,000', '$15,000', '$50,000'],
 'Rule 4530(a)(1)(G) uses a $15,000 threshold for claims against an associated person and $25,000 when the member is the defendant, respondent or subject of the claim.'),
('A firm suspends a representative for two weeks for marking orders unsolicited when they were solicited. Under Rule 4530(a)(2) the firm must:',
 'Report the internal discipline to FINRA', ['Report it only if a customer complains about it', 'Note it only in the next branch inspection report', 'Report it only if the person later resigns'],
 "Rule 4530(a)(2) requires a member to report when it disciplines an associated person with a suspension, termination, withholding of commissions or a fine over $2,500, or otherwise significantly limits the person's activities."),
('In FINRA customer arbitration, a claim for $40,000 is normally decided by:',
 'One arbitrator on the papers, unless she asks for a hearing', ['A three-person panel after a full in-person hearing in her city', 'A FINRA Hearing Panel in a disciplinary case', 'A federal judge sitting without a jury'],
 'Under Rule 12800, simplified arbitration for claims of $50,000 or less is decided by one arbitrator on the pleadings and documents unless the customer requests a hearing.'),
("Under the Industry Code, an employee's claim of employment discrimination under a statute is arbitrated in FINRA's forum:",
 'Only if the parties agreed to arbitrate it', ['Always, since all industry disputes must be arbitrated', 'Never, since FINRA cannot hear any such claim', 'Only if the employee is a registered principal'],
 'Rule 13201 says a statutory employment discrimination claim is not required to be arbitrated under the Code; it can be arbitrated only if the parties agreed to do so, before or after the dispute arose.'),
('A customer asks for a copy of the predispute arbitration agreement she signed. Under Rule 2268 the firm must provide it within:',
 '10 business days of the request', ['24 hours of the request', '30 calendar days of the request', 'The next account statement cycle'],
 'Rule 2268 requires a member to give the customer a copy of the predispute arbitration agreement within ten business days of receiving the request, and the agreement must carry the required highlighted disclosures.'),
('A former representative who left the industry a year ago ignores a FINRA Rule 8210 request for testimony. FINRA most likely:',
 'May bar the person from the industry', ['Has no power over a former representative at all', 'Must ask the SEC to issue a subpoena', 'Can only send a letter of caution'],
 'FINRA keeps jurisdiction over a person for two years after termination (By-Laws Article V, Section 4). Failing to respond to a Rule 8210 request is a serious violation that commonly leads to a bar.'),
('Under the FINRA By-Laws, FINRA keeps jurisdiction to bring a disciplinary action against a former associated person for:',
 'Two years after the registration ends', ['One year after the registration ends', 'Six years after the registration ends', 'As long as the person is alive'],
 'Article V, Section 4 of the FINRA By-Laws retains jurisdiction for two years after the effective date of termination of registration, measured as the rule sets out.'),
('A firm wants to appeal a FINRA Hearing Panel decision in a disciplinary case. The first appeal goes to:',
 'The National Adjudicatory Council', ['The Securities and Exchange Commission', 'A federal district court', 'A FINRA arbitration panel'],
 'Under the Rule 9300 Series a Hearing Panel decision can be appealed to the National Adjudicatory Council. After that a party may seek SEC review, and then go to a federal court of appeals.'),
('SEC Rule 17a-4, as amended in 2022, lets a firm keep required electronic records on a system that either prevents changes or:',
 'Keeps a time-stamped audit trail of every change', ['Prints a paper copy of each record once a year', "Stores the records on each representative's own laptop", 'Deletes drafts as soon as final copies exist'],
 'Rule 17a-4(f) now allows an electronic recordkeeping system that either preserves records in a non-rewriteable, non-erasable format or keeps a complete time-stamped audit trail that lets the original be recreated after any change.'),
]
